! =============================================================================
! SaltFoss Training — Segment 3 (0:16-0:28): The chemical potential trap (3/3)
! =============================================================================
! Remedy #2: fuzzy stoichiometry. Instead of hand-perturbing a mass, set
! fuzzy = .TRUE. and Thermochimica adds a small random perturbation
! (+/- dFuzzMag, default 1e-12) to each nonzero entry of the stoichiometry
! matrix before solving (src/setup/RandomizeStoichiometry.f90). Composition
! here is EXACT (F=4.0, same as 02a) -- the fuzz, not the input, breaks the
! degeneracy.
!
! CAVEAT (from the user manual): fuzzy stoichiometry can introduce small
! amounts of spurious trace phases. Always inspect post-processed output.
!
! Run:    ./bin/InputScriptMode inputs/training/saltfoss/02c_fuzzy.ti
! Verified output (kJ/mol): mu_F=-97.9  mu_Be=-927.1  mu_Li=-574.2
!   -> mu(LiF) = -672.10    mu(BeF2) = -1122.95
! Matches 02b_perturbed.ti essentially exactly, and the species combinations
! still match 02a to <0.1 kJ/mol.
! =============================================================================
temperature       = 900
pressure          = 1.0
mass(3)           = 2.0        ! Li
mass(4)           = 1.0        ! Be
mass(9)           = 4.0        ! F  -- EXACT, same as 02a
temperature unit  = K
pressure unit     = atm
mass unit         = moles
data file         = data/MSD-TC_V4.1_Fluorides_No_Func.dat
print mode        = 2
fuzzy             = .TRUE.
